  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\n\nShowers and storms will be ongoing Thursday morning, tapering off by \nthe afternoon. Highs for most areas cool to the upper 70s and 80s, \nwith a few spots reaching 90F along our southern border. Will see \nmore redevelopment of showers and storms by Thursday evening into \nFriday (50 to 80% chance along and north of the Platte River) as \ncontinued warm advection and another mid level impulse moves into \nthe area. Some severe potential exists too, largely over our \nsouthern area where the best shear and instability overlap.\n\nPeriodic shower and storm chances are forecast for much of the \nextended as the H5 ridge finally pushes toward the southeast CONUS, \nplacing us in southwesterly flow with several disturbances moving \nthrough. At this time, the best chances appear to be Friday night \ninto Saturday (30-50%) and Saturday night into Sunday (50-70%). \nHighs Friday and Saturday warm to the 80s/low 90s, while by Sunday \nand Monday, cooler temps arrive in the mid 70s to low 80s.",
